   The af2rank class in predict_af2rank.py is taken from the AF2Rank example
   notebook distributed with ColabDesign (af/examples/AF2Rank.ipynb) and
   modified for this repository. save_recycles.py subclasses its
   mk_af_model and reproduces part of the run method of its _af_design class.
   One hunk of patches/01-evoformer-capture.patch modifies its
   colabdesign/af/model.py.

2. AlphaFold (https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphafold), Copyright 2021
   DeepMind Technologies Limited, is licensed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0, and ColabDesign includes it. The remaining hunks of
   patches/01-evoformer-capture.patch modify three of those files:
   colabdesign/af/alphafold/model/layer_stack.py, modules.py and
   modules_multimer.py.

The methods this code builds on are described in:
  AlphaFold2: J. Jumper, R. Evans, A. Pritzel, et al., Nature 596, 583-589
    (2021).
  AlphaFold-Multimer: R. Evans, M. O'Neill, A. Pritzel, et al., bioRxiv (2022),
    doi:10.1101/2021.10.04.463034.
  AF2Rank: J. P. Roney and S. Ovchinnikov, Phys. Rev. Lett. 129, 238101 (2022).

AlphaFold2 and AlphaFold-Multimer network parameters are not distributed here.
They are released by DeepMind under CC BY 4.0 and are fetched separately; see
README.md.

The structures under example/ relate to Protein Data Bank entries 1IRA and
1R8S, as distributed with the Protein-Protein Docking Benchmark 5.5. Each
native.pdb is that experimental structure, and the files under
templates_predicted-monomers/ were produced by docking monomers taken from an
AlphaFold-Multimer prediction of the same target.
